# Source: Gastronomy.md

## Key Entities
- **Gastronomy Portal** — Navigation hub for food/cooking content (central, new)
- **Wok Cooking, Wok Hei, Maillard Reaction, Flavor Theory, Ingredient Pairings, Aromatics, Seasonings, Salmon Collars** — Core concepts/pages linked from portal (central, most already exist in wiki)
- **Recipe: Perfect Stir-Fry, Recipe: Glazed Salmon Collars, Recipe: Umami Building Blocks** — Recipe pages likely not yet in wiki (peripheral, new)
- **Resource: Salt Fat Acid Heat, Resource:The Flavor Bible, Resource:Wok Cooking Masterclass** — Learning resources, likely new (peripheral, new)
- **Salmon** — Ingredient page, likely new (peripheral, new)

## Key Concepts
- **Wok Hei** — "Breath of the wok," the charred flavor from high-heat wok cooking (already exists)
- **Maillard Reaction** — Browning reaction that builds flavor (already exists)
- **Flavor Theory** — Understanding taste combinations (already exists)
- **Ingredient Pairings** — What ingredients work together (already exists)
- **Resting Meat** — Juiciness maximization technique (new)
- **Umami Building Blocks** — Likely a concept about foundational umami flavor construction (new)

## Main Arguments & Findings
This is a navigation portal, not a source with arguments. It organizes existing and anticipated cooking knowledge into categories (Techniques, Recipes, Ingredients, Flavor Profiles). No empirical claims.

## Connections to Existing Wiki
Strong overlap with existing pages: [[wok-cooking]], [[wok-hei]], [[maillard-reaction]], [[flavor-theory]], [[ingredient-pairings]], [[aromatics]], [[aromatics-the-holy-trinity]], [[salmon-collars]], [[category-cooking-techniques]], [[rice-varieties-index]] (implied), and several cuisine pages. The portal consolidates scattered food content into a single entry point.

## Contradictions & Tensions
None. This is a neutral organizing structure.

## Recommendations
- **Create/update**: The portal page itself is new and should be added as a hub. Several linked recipe and resource pages need creation (Recipe: Perfect Stir-Fry, Recipe: Glazed Salmon Collars, Recipe: Umami Building Blocks, Resource: Salt Fat Acid Heat, etc.).
- **Emphasize**: The connection to existing flavor theory, wok techniques, and Maillard reaction content. The portal strengthens the food/cooking knowledge cluster.
- **Flag**: Resting Meat and Umami Building Blocks are novel concepts not yet in the wiki — worth developing. Also check whether [[aromatics-the-holy-trinity]] should be linked from the portal since it exists.
- **De-emphasize**: Nothing here conflicts with existing content.
- **Open questions**: Are the recipe and resource pages intended to be authored, or are they placeholder links?
